Debian/Ubuntu packaging for the fsevent module
=============================================

qore-fsevent-module contains the native watcher, FsEventPoller and
FsEventPollerUtil, both Qore sources and compiled qmods, and all compiler
metadata. qore-fsevent-module-doc contains the three API references and tests.
Debhelper creates matching debug symbols for all three ELF modules.

Build prerequisites and supported scope
--------------------------------------

Use an isolated native build environment with the packaged Qore runtime and
libqore-dev, then install the Build-Depends from debian/control. Qualification
currently targets Ubuntu 26.04 amd64 with Qore 3.0 development packages. Other
Debian/Ubuntu releases and architectures need their own qualified SDK and native
testing. Cross builds are rejected because Qore tools run during compilation.

The bundled efsw implementation is private to the module. It includes Qore's
watcher-destruction fixes (including commit 846ba83), threading changes and
portability fixes; substituting an unpatched library would lose those changes.
There is no efsw development package in the qualified distribution. No separate
efsw library is installed. Its MIT license and the embedded SFML/Zlib and
public-domain notices are included in debian/copyright.

Native Qore modules resolve libqore symbols at load time without linking it.
The package therefore derives a minimum libqore SONAME package and qore version
from the SDK used to build it. Other shared-library dependencies come from
dh_shlibdeps. The package requires the native interpreter, includes architecture
specific qmods and shared metadata, and is not marked Multi-Arch: same.

AOT modules and debug symbols
----------------------------

The build explicitly enables AOT modules, disables source-tree qmod symlinks,
and honors the noopt build option for Qore compilation. Distribution prefix maps
are passed through the SDK's CMake macros for reproducible qmods and metadata.
Only the new native module, new qmods and packaged Qore standard library are
used by build-time tests. All three modules remain in the runtime package.

dh_strip must preserve Qore's appended dependency/source-location/optional-module
metadata. debian/preserve-aot-metadata.py is copied from Qore's qualified
packaging and wraps all stripping/debug-link operations. Its real-ELF unit tests
run during package builds. dwz skips this runtime package because it does not
understand all LLVM DWARF forms; dh_strip still creates matching debug packages.
Do not replace this handling with ordinary stripping or omit AOT trailers.

Source and binary builds
------------------------

Use a fresh version for every changed upload. This snapshot precedes 2.0.0.
From a clean committed checkout:

    version=2.0.0~git20260928.1
    mkdir -p ../fsevent-package-work
    git archive --format=tar --prefix="qore-fsevent-module-$version/" \
        HEAD -- . ':!debian' | xz > \
        "../fsevent-package-work/qore-fsevent-module_$version.orig.tar.xz"
    tar -xf "../fsevent-package-work/qore-fsevent-module_$version.orig.tar.xz" \
        -C ../fsevent-package-work
    cp -a debian "../fsevent-package-work/qore-fsevent-module-$version/"
    cd "../fsevent-package-work/qore-fsevent-module-$version"
    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc

Extract the .dsc with dpkg-source -x into a clean build directory. Install all
build dependencies and build unprivileged with networking disabled:

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

Architecture-only builds (-B) do not need Doxygen; architecture-independent
builds (-A) produce documentation. Both DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nodoc and
DEB_BUILD_PROFILES=nodoc suppress docs; the profile also omits the doc package.
Do not use nocheck for qualification.

Qualification and publication
-----------------------------

Run all seven upstream suites, including callback destruction, negative cases,
filesystem watching and both Qore modules. The tests resolve modules by name;
source-tree users can use ../qlib, while installed tests copy only test scripts
and explicitly preload the installed qmods, with no source directory available.
The compiler test configures a native watcher with named method arguments and checks
the event data type registered by FsEventPollerUtil in a fresh executable.
No external service or optional Qore module is required.

Check source/binary Lintian, all three ELF modules' hardening, matching DWARF
and Qore trailers, runtime-only install without SDK, docs/debug coinstallation,
dpkg -V, purge/reinstall and reproducibility in two distinct build directories.
Retain source/package hashes, the commit, dependency inventory and test logs.
Testing-PPA publication is separate from approval for a final general release.
